# PROJECT: UNIVERSE — A GLOBAL UNIVERSITY CONFESSION & STUDENT COMMUNITY PLATFORM

Act as a senior full-stack developer, UI/UX designer, product designer, and software architect.

Build a complete, responsive, interactive university community website called "UniVerse." The name must be easy to change later.

This is a student-centered platform where university students from around the world can share anonymous confessions, communicate with other students, exchange academic notes, recommend places near their universities, create cute avatars, and customize the entire website to their personal taste.

The website must look like a professionally designed, production-quality application. Do not create a generic AI-looking landing page, a basic dashboard template, or a static mockup.

I want a real project with multiple pages, reusable components, a proper folder structure, working navigation, functional interactions, and a consistent design system.

The project must be downloadable or exportable as a complete folder that I can open in Visual Studio Code and run locally.

Do not put the entire application into one HTML file.

