# 6. BUILT-IN AI CONFESSION ANALYZER

Create an AI-powered classification service.

When a user submits a confession, analyze its text and determine:

* Primary category.
* Optional secondary category.
* Sentiment.
* General topic.
* Whether it is a question.
* Whether it is seeking advice.
* Whether it appears to contain personal information.
* Whether it may violate community rules.

Use the results to organize the confession feed and assist moderation.

## Example

Input:

"I have a crush on someone in my lecture, but I have no idea how to start talking to them."

Expected classification:

{
"category": "Love & Crushes",
"secondaryCategory": "Advice",
"sentiment": "Nervous",
"topic": "University relationships",
"isQuestion": true,
"needsAdvice": true,
"moderationStatus": "Review"
}

The exact classification must depend on the content.

## AI implementation requirements

Use a structured JSON response from the model.

Validate the output before using it.

Use a server-side API endpoint for AI requests.

Never expose private AI API keys in frontend code or public environment variables.

Use environment variables for credentials.

If a Gemini API integration is used, implement it through a secure server-side service.

If AI is not configured, provide a functional local fallback classifier using keyword rules.

The application must still run without an AI API key.

Do not pretend the fallback classifier is a real AI model.

Display an appropriate label in development mode.

## Moderation requirements

The AI must not automatically label every accusation as factual.

Potentially harmful posts should be held for review rather than automatically published.

Create a moderation status system:

* Pending.
* Published.
* Needs Review.
* Rejected.

Allow community administrators to review flagged content.

Do not infer sensitive personal characteristics from confessions.

Do not use sentiment classification to diagnose mental health conditions.

